# Quote flanking after a slash

## Root cause

The inline parser treats a slash as an opening context for a straight quote. Its follow-up rule for closing quotes after a dash does not include slash. A quote after the final slash in a path therefore opens when the next character is punctuation or the end of the inline source.

## Change

Apply the existing dash follow-up rule to slash. Keep the same next-character classification for both characters. When Djot explicitly forces an opening single quote after a slash, spell that imported quote as the opening glyph so the generic parser rule cannot reverse it. Add parser and importer regressions for both contexts.

## Scope

This changes quote direction based on the neighboring characters, not on any path, URL, or corpus spelling. Djot's explicit opening quote remains an opening quote. The rule covers every slash followed by a straight quote under the normative typography rule.
